--TEST--
an assertion names `$actual` before `$expected`, a trailing `{message: ...}` is written in front of that report, `assertEqualsDeep` names the path of the first difference, and `assertThrows` consumes the throw (`rule:testing/assertions-are-typed`, `rule:testing/failure-ledger`)
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:testing/assertions
// `rule:testing/failure-ledger`: a failure is an ordinary `Throwable`, so
// outside a `#[Test]` method an arm around the call is all it takes to read
// the message the runner would have reported.
use Core\Test;

// `rule:testing/assertions-are-typed`: subject first. A reversed call reads
// correctly because both sides are named rather than positional.
try {
    Test::assertSame(2 + 2, 5);
} catch (Core\Test\Failure $f) {
    echo $f->message, "\n";
}

// The written message is a prefix of the report, not a replacement for it.
try {
    Test::assertTrue(false, {message: "a fresh counter is one"});
} catch (Core\Test\Failure $f) {
    echo $f->message, "\n";
}

// A deep comparison names the path it stopped at, so a difference inside a
// large value is located rather than only reported.
array<string> $sent = ["city" => "Berlin", "zip" => "10115"];
array<string> $stored = ["city" => "Berlin", "zip" => "10117"];
try {
    Test::assertEqualsDeep($sent, $stored);
} catch (Core\Test\Failure $f) {
    echo $f->message, "\n";
}

// The throw `assertThrows` was given is consumed, so the statement after it
// runs. A subclass of the named class holds.
Test::assertThrows(fn (): void => { throw new ParseError("bad input"); }, RuntimeError::class);
echo "the ParseError was consumed\n";

// An assertion that holds returns nothing and lets the program carry on.
Test::assertDoesNotThrow(fn (): void => { echo "the body ran\n"; });
echo "done\n";
--EXPECT--
Core\Test::assertSame failed: `$actual` is 4, `$expected` is 5
a fresh counter is one: Core\Test::assertTrue failed: `$actual` is false
Core\Test::assertEqualsDeep failed: the two differ at `$actual["zip"]`: `$actual` is "10115", `$expected` is "10117"
the ParseError was consumed
the body ran
done
